WEBVTT

00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:38.280
The Professor I Don't Know

00:01:36.670 --> 00:01:39.690
Won't you have a little chat with me?

00:01:40.490 --> 00:01:43.570
I must decline. I am quite busy today.

00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:46.570
Now, now, don't be that way.

00:01:46.570 --> 00:01:48.870
I said I am busy.

00:01:49.830 --> 00:01:53.590
Don't be so guarded.
It isn't like I'm going to kidnap you.

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:55.700
You are kidnapping me as we speak.

00:01:55.700 --> 00:01:57.130
Hmph!

00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:04.680
Don't panic.
I'll deliver you safely to the palace.

00:02:07.190 --> 00:02:10.720
I've wanted to chat with
you for a long time now.

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:14.390
I've heard all about you from my cousin.

00:02:14.390 --> 00:02:15.310
Your cousin?

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:17.440
Maximilian, the palace guard.

00:02:18.050 --> 00:02:20.060
There's a slight resemblance, isn't there?

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:24.440
Their ambiance couldn't be more different,
but they do look slightly alike.

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:27.070
In our sunny dispositions.

00:02:27.070 --> 00:02:28.710
Hello, Professor!

00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:30.340
That?

00:02:30.340 --> 00:02:35.160
He says he envies how you and
the princes are very close.

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:40.130
Indeed, the princes have changed
quite a lot since you arrived.

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:41.940
In a good way.

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:46.830
I must admit that I also wished
to have a longer talk with you.

00:02:47.610 --> 00:02:50.470
Every time the princes have a problem...

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:53.730
you are always moving behind it.

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:56.030
I certainly wasn't expecting that.

00:02:56.030 --> 00:02:58.020
No need to feign ignorance.

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:01.110
You attempted to aggravate
the matter with Prince Licht

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:03.700
by telling His Majesty about
the prince's job in town.

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:05.100
With Prince Bruno...

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:08.750
The probability that you could become
king is, well, zero, isn't it?

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:12.950
You tried to dissuade him from the path
to the throne using Dr. Dmitri.

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:14.800
With Prince Kai, as well...

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:17.160
I don't know what you're referring to.

00:03:17.810 --> 00:03:22.410
Have you ever met a boy
named Ralf von Fuchs?

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:23.170
Ralf?

00:03:23.490 --> 00:03:27.190
The instigator behind the violent incident
Prince Kai was pulled into.

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:31.670
Supposedly, he heard accusatory gossip about
the princes from a family acquaintance.

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:36.560
And you believe that I
breathed it into his ears?

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:38.480
I believe it is a possibility.

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:43.790
I do have a friend by the
name of Adam von Fuchs.

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:46.330
I suppose they could be relatives.

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:50.910
But I have never met this Ralf.

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:53.830
Now, if you suspect I am causing trouble

00:03:53.830 --> 00:03:57.040
for the younger princes to
keep them from the crown,

00:03:57.070 --> 00:03:59.080
you are barking up the wrong tree.

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:05.580
Prince Eins is the eldest. He is distinguished.
He excels in cultural and military pursuits.

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:09.030
Everyone says that he will be the next king.

00:04:09.030 --> 00:04:11.590
You are implying that there
is no need to get in the way?

00:04:11.590 --> 00:04:14.710
Yes. But enough about that, Professor.

00:04:15.010 --> 00:04:19.660
Would you be so kind as to tell
me your thoughts on this article?

00:04:20.070 --> 00:04:24.990
I thought you might have an idea
about the identity of this criminal.

00:04:25.610 --> 00:04:28.180
Oh, dear. We're already at the palace.

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:31.380
Time flies when you're having fun.

00:04:32.420 --> 00:04:35.040
We'll have to continue this
conversation another day.

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:38.020
Heine!

00:04:39.050 --> 00:04:42.260
Prince Leonhard. What is it?

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:44.220
Erm, um...

00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:46.380
Ah, yes. Professor!

00:04:47.070 --> 00:04:51.630
I forgot to mention something. I found out...

00:04:51.870 --> 00:04:53.390
who you really are.

00:04:54.760 --> 00:04:59.390
I hear you tutored children at a
church before coming to the palace.

00:04:59.670 --> 00:05:02.980
A little church called Maria Vetsera.

00:05:02.980 --> 00:05:08.400
An interesting fact came out when I looked
into the reason you were teaching there.

00:05:09.640 --> 00:05:13.700
What I mean to say is...
You are not from our side, are you?

00:05:16.530 --> 00:05:17.560
Our side?

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:22.040
I would love to hear more
about it when next we meet.

00:05:22.040 --> 00:05:24.190
Now, I'd best be off.

00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:27.250
Prince Leonhard. Shall we?

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:30.270
Our side? A church? What's this about?

00:05:30.810 --> 00:05:31.470
Huh?

00:05:31.820 --> 00:05:32.930
Heine?

00:05:43.290 --> 00:05:45.090
Is something the matter, Your Highness?

00:05:46.150 --> 00:05:48.230
Where did you spring out from?!

00:05:48.230 --> 00:05:51.530
How rude. I only circled behind you.

00:05:51.530 --> 00:05:52.730
An opening!

00:05:52.970 --> 00:05:54.460
Why are you running?

00:05:54.950 --> 00:05:57.360
Wait, Prince Leonhard!

00:05:59.170 --> 00:06:01.590
Stare

00:05:59.390 --> 00:06:01.590
Stare...

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:10.680
Stare

00:06:08.420 --> 00:06:10.370
Stare...

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:24.270
Irritation

00:06:11.040 --> 00:06:15.910
Ahem. Is there something you would
very much like to say to me?

00:06:15.910 --> 00:06:17.620
What?! Why, you...

00:06:17.620 --> 00:06:19.320
What made you think that
when you looked at me?

00:06:19.320 --> 00:06:21.860
Everything. Now spit it out, please.

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:24.270
W-Well, ahem, that is...

00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:28.230
You taught at a church? What's the
meaning of this? I never heard of this!

00:06:28.550 --> 00:06:30.300
Well, no, because I never told you.

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:31.090
Why not?!

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:32.470
You never asked.

00:06:32.470 --> 00:06:33.530
Don't you split hairs!

00:06:33.750 --> 00:06:36.440
A long time ago, I was a volunteer tutor.

00:06:36.440 --> 00:06:38.820
Then you taught without being paid?

00:06:39.090 --> 00:06:41.670
Your Highness, you know what
"volunteer" means? Excellent.

00:06:41.940 --> 00:06:43.820
D-Don't make fun of me!

00:06:43.820 --> 00:06:51.080
I was not paid for it, but the church did
thank me with a meal for each day's work.

00:06:51.390 --> 00:06:55.360
I see... So you had
students other than us...

00:06:55.930 --> 00:07:00.140
Ahem. Were you looking
for me to give me that?

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:01.500
Yes. So what?

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:03.730
Was there a problem you needed help with?

00:07:03.730 --> 00:07:08.200
Or did you completely give up,
unable to read even the question sheet?

00:07:08.200 --> 00:07:10.470
N-No! It's the opposite!

00:07:10.470 --> 00:07:11.150
My word.

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:13.360
You were studying ahead?

00:07:13.360 --> 00:07:16.950
That's right! Sometimes I want to study.

00:07:16.950 --> 00:07:18.740
I worked ahead as I pleased. You're welcome.

00:07:19.560 --> 00:07:22.490
Well, this is incredible.
I can tell you worked hard.

00:07:23.780 --> 00:07:28.560
Go ahead, then! Feel all pleased
that your student has grown.

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:29.790
Why is he acting haughty?

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:35.250
I will take this and grade
it in time for your lesson.

00:07:36.360 --> 00:07:39.600
Hmph. That's right, work for me!

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:41.110
Really, why does he insist
on acting haughty?

00:07:45.190 --> 00:07:48.300
Prince Leonhard, you have truly grown...

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:51.130
Hey! Hey! Teacher! Teacher!

00:07:51.130 --> 00:07:52.030
Hmm?

00:07:54.380 --> 00:07:57.270
If there's anything you don't understand,
raise your hands.

00:07:57.270 --> 00:07:58.070
Now, children...

00:07:58.070 --> 00:08:00.080
Try to solve the next problem.

00:08:00.290 --> 00:08:01.810
Okay!

00:08:01.810 --> 00:08:03.530
It's Professor Heine!

00:08:03.530 --> 00:08:04.480
Master!

00:08:04.480 --> 00:08:05.360
Master?

00:08:05.360 --> 00:08:06.350
Professor Heine?

00:08:06.350 --> 00:08:09.040
Children, stop chatting and
concentrate on the problem.

00:08:09.310 --> 00:08:10.540
Okay.

00:08:09.350 --> 00:08:13.890
Prince Bruno, a corrected article about
the incident was published this morning.

00:08:14.240 --> 00:08:15.930
Have you seen it?

00:08:15.930 --> 00:08:19.340
Yes. I'm in a radiant mood because of it.

00:08:19.340 --> 00:08:20.800
Glad to hear it.

00:08:22.170 --> 00:08:26.270
You're teaching children? That's excellent.

00:08:26.270 --> 00:08:27.970
Thank you.

00:08:27.980 --> 00:08:32.360
I was wondering if there was anything else
I needed to learn as a candidate for king,

00:08:32.360 --> 00:08:35.360
when Adele asked me to teach her.

00:08:35.760 --> 00:08:37.650
That was my eureka moment.

00:08:37.990 --> 00:08:40.080
I want to cultivate a relationship
with the children,

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:43.160
and become a king who is needed
by multiple generations!

00:08:43.160 --> 00:08:43.920
So I thought. Only...

00:08:43.920 --> 00:08:45.410
Brother, are you done yet?

00:08:45.410 --> 00:08:47.290
What do princes do every day?

00:08:47.290 --> 00:08:49.070
Do you like dogs or cats?

00:08:49.070 --> 00:08:51.050
What's your least favorite food?

00:08:51.050 --> 00:08:53.960
Prince Bruno, do you have a girlfriend?

00:08:53.960 --> 00:08:54.800
Eek!

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:58.090
A-A girlfriend? Wh-What are you...

00:08:58.530 --> 00:09:01.000
No questions that aren't
related to the lesson!

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:02.680
Aww.

00:09:03.170 --> 00:09:08.680
As you can see, the lesson is hardly coming
together. We have wasted a lot of time.

00:09:09.370 --> 00:09:12.930
If Your Highness cannot
lead this many children...

00:09:12.930 --> 00:09:17.690
How can you hope to lead millions
of subjects as a king?

00:09:17.690 --> 00:09:18.520
Wh...

00:09:19.330 --> 00:09:21.600
To become a leader,

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:25.090
you must have an appealing temperament,
or no one will follow you.

00:09:25.090 --> 00:09:30.410
It's true. I decided to follow you upon
learning what an incredible person you are.

00:09:30.760 --> 00:09:32.470
Master! Thank you!

00:09:34.390 --> 00:09:36.970
I will take your advice
to heart and try again!

00:09:42.710 --> 00:09:47.400
Boys and girls! I want to begin class today
by having you learn more about me.

00:09:47.400 --> 00:09:48.800
To answer your questions...

00:09:48.800 --> 00:09:51.020
Unfortunately, I have no girlfriend.

00:09:51.330 --> 00:09:54.100
I prefer dogs to cats.
We have a pet dog, after all.

00:09:54.100 --> 00:09:56.660
I spend my days reading and studying.

00:09:56.660 --> 00:09:59.470
If I had to choose a least favorite food,
I'd say it's liver.

00:09:58.200 --> 00:10:02.800
Prince Bruno, it is excellent that
you are so accepting of advice.

00:09:59.470 --> 00:10:00.780
Liver is disgusting.

00:10:02.190 --> 00:10:03.470
I like it!

00:10:05.100 --> 00:10:06.920
It's very soft.

00:10:06.920 --> 00:10:08.170
Oh, really?

00:10:07.250 --> 00:10:08.170
Soft...

00:10:10.850 --> 00:10:12.950
Prince Kai, too, has completely settled in.

00:10:13.410 --> 00:10:14.490
Professor.

00:10:14.860 --> 00:10:16.000
Do you have a moment?

00:10:16.280 --> 00:10:17.900
What can I do for you?

00:10:19.660 --> 00:10:22.480
I see. You wish to return
to military school?

00:10:22.480 --> 00:10:25.220
Yeah. After what happened,

00:10:25.220 --> 00:10:29.010
I thought I should never go
to school again and gave up.

00:10:29.010 --> 00:10:33.020
But now that the truth is known,
I want to try going back.

00:10:33.370 --> 00:10:36.100
Do you now? Have you told your father?

00:10:36.750 --> 00:10:40.780
No. I know he'll be against it.

00:10:40.780 --> 00:10:44.860
But... I'm happy that I can speak
to the people at the palace now.

00:10:45.110 --> 00:10:48.800
The people at school might not all be nice.

00:10:49.210 --> 00:10:54.390
But I think what I need now is to be
able to interact with not-nice people.

00:10:55.920 --> 00:10:59.610
That is an excellent attitude, Prince Kai.

00:11:00.170 --> 00:11:02.760
However, instead of having me help,

00:11:02.760 --> 00:11:06.180
perhaps you should try to persuade
your father on your own?

00:11:06.730 --> 00:11:10.360
You will need that kind of
strength to become king.

00:11:10.360 --> 00:11:12.270
Yeah. You might be right.

00:11:12.270 --> 00:11:13.600
I know you can do it.

00:11:14.040 --> 00:11:15.430
Do your best.

00:11:19.690 --> 00:11:22.610
Sorry you always have to
come with me, Professor.

00:11:22.610 --> 00:11:25.910
Not at all. There are many
things for you to learn here.

00:11:26.490 --> 00:11:29.810
I am honored to be able
to assist you with that.

00:11:30.610 --> 00:11:32.410
Richard!

00:11:32.410 --> 00:11:34.370
Let's chat again.

00:11:34.670 --> 00:11:37.770
My, my. You're quite popular
with these lovely ladies.

00:11:37.770 --> 00:11:41.490
Yup! When I talk to them, I learn a lot.

00:11:41.490 --> 00:11:43.750
Like that there are places
that need more doctors,

00:11:43.750 --> 00:11:46.940
that land is jumping in price,
and educational problems and whatnot.

00:11:46.940 --> 00:11:51.060
Like, the societal problems of the
season feel real to me now, I guess?

00:11:51.270 --> 00:11:54.020
Oh? You have matured, haven't you?

00:11:54.260 --> 00:11:57.070
I'm the super hot prince of charisma.

00:11:57.510 --> 00:11:58.470
Of course I have!

00:11:58.470 --> 00:12:00.770
Hey, don't keep us waiting!

00:12:00.770 --> 00:12:01.650
I'm coming!

00:12:01.650 --> 00:12:06.170
Your Highness, please continue to push
forward on a path you believe in.

00:12:06.170 --> 00:12:09.160
Sheesh, you make it sound
like we're saying goodbye.

00:12:09.160 --> 00:12:10.800
Well, see you later!

00:12:14.810 --> 00:12:15.490
Yes.

00:12:21.750 --> 00:12:25.590
I found out who you really are.

00:12:25.790 --> 00:12:28.710
You are not from our side, are you?

00:12:30.990 --> 00:12:34.550
If my past ever comes to light...

00:12:34.550 --> 00:12:40.410
I remember. That was your condition
for becoming the royal tutor.

00:12:51.580 --> 00:12:57.460
Oh, yeah. Apparently Heine used to teach
children in a church as a volunteer.

00:12:57.460 --> 00:12:59.540
A church? That's news to me!

00:12:59.800 --> 00:13:01.590
Yeah... here, too...

00:13:01.590 --> 00:13:03.040
Who told you this?

00:13:03.040 --> 00:13:04.760
You know, that one guy.

00:13:05.310 --> 00:13:08.510
Robe... Ro... Rorberobe...

00:13:08.510 --> 00:13:08.830
Ro...

00:13:08.830 --> 00:13:09.960
Count Rosenberg!

00:13:10.590 --> 00:13:12.720
Bruno, how did you know?!

00:13:13.130 --> 00:13:13.970
That guy?

00:13:15.140 --> 00:13:18.510
He said he'd figured out who Heine
really is or something, too.

00:13:18.510 --> 00:13:22.890
Then he spouted some confusing stuff
about Heine not being from our side.

00:13:23.160 --> 00:13:26.460
Who he really is? Our side?
What does it all mean?

00:13:27.910 --> 00:13:32.530
Come of think of it, we know barely
anything about the professor.

00:13:32.750 --> 00:13:37.110
You said it. I've asked
him before, but no dice.

00:13:37.110 --> 00:13:39.710
You can ask him face-to-face but
there's no way he'd answer.

00:13:39.710 --> 00:13:43.170
Actually, I also looked into Master's past.

00:13:43.170 --> 00:13:45.000
I couldn't find out anything.

00:13:45.210 --> 00:13:48.180
Oh, how about we try his room, then?

00:13:48.180 --> 00:13:50.260
We might find some clues.

00:13:50.260 --> 00:13:54.010
Then now's our chance. He said he'd be
going to the bookstore in the morning.

00:13:54.010 --> 00:13:56.640
It's impolite to enter his
room while he's absent.

00:13:56.850 --> 00:13:58.670
Then you don't have to come.

00:13:58.670 --> 00:13:59.010
What?

00:13:59.010 --> 00:14:01.770
I wonder that Heine's room is like?
I can't wait to see!

00:14:01.280 --> 00:14:01.770
Ah...

00:14:02.030 --> 00:14:04.130
And that's that. Kai, you come, too.

00:14:04.130 --> 00:14:04.630
Okay.

00:14:04.130 --> 00:14:05.490
W-Wait...

00:14:04.630 --> 00:14:06.780
I bet there'll be lots of books
we've never seen before!

00:14:05.490 --> 00:14:08.780
I cannot let you rummage
through Master's room.

00:14:06.780 --> 00:14:08.560
I bet we'll dig up the most amazing things.

00:14:08.560 --> 00:14:09.570
Like what? Like what?

00:14:09.570 --> 00:14:10.960
I'm going, too!

00:14:13.420 --> 00:14:14.970
Professor, are you there?

00:14:14.970 --> 00:14:16.140
Is he out?

00:14:16.140 --> 00:14:17.650
Seems like he's gone.

00:14:17.650 --> 00:14:19.380
Shall we let ourselves in?

00:14:19.860 --> 00:14:21.790
Did you need me?

00:14:22.230 --> 00:14:23.310
Heine!

00:14:23.540 --> 00:14:25.970
I-I need homework help.

00:14:25.970 --> 00:14:27.630
S-So do I.

00:14:30.060 --> 00:14:32.190
Do you now? Please, come in.

00:14:34.430 --> 00:14:36.280
O-Oh, my God...

00:14:36.280 --> 00:14:37.090
Heine.

00:14:38.400 --> 00:14:39.220
Yes?

00:14:39.220 --> 00:14:40.810
Your room is...

00:14:40.810 --> 00:14:42.170
A mess!

00:14:43.600 --> 00:14:46.260
Don't, Leo! You can't describe
it exactly as it looks!

00:14:46.260 --> 00:14:49.190
Licht! It's obviously rude
to be that honest about it!

00:14:49.480 --> 00:14:50.520
Sulk...

00:14:51.230 --> 00:14:53.780
A-Ahem. What a lovely room.

00:14:54.330 --> 00:14:57.810
Especially this table set in the
shape of books. It's so whimsical.

00:14:57.810 --> 00:14:59.900
That is a bona fide stack of books.

00:14:59.900 --> 00:15:01.790
F-Forgive me, Master.

00:15:02.240 --> 00:15:04.770
I've been busy working lately.

00:15:04.770 --> 00:15:07.410
I've had no time to tidy my room.

00:15:08.740 --> 00:15:10.050
Wait, is that...

00:15:10.050 --> 00:15:11.680
...my fault?

00:15:17.470 --> 00:15:20.850
Professor's room cleaning squad! Mobilize!

00:15:23.840 --> 00:15:25.720
Cleaning squad?

00:15:26.420 --> 00:15:31.190
Our studies can wait. To show you our
gratitude for all your work for us,

00:15:31.190 --> 00:15:33.570
we will clean your room from top to bottom!

00:15:33.570 --> 00:15:34.490
Worrisome.

00:15:34.720 --> 00:15:36.810
Master! The plan is perfect!

00:15:36.810 --> 00:15:38.740
I've devised the most
efficient course of action.

00:15:38.740 --> 00:15:39.490
Question!

00:15:39.490 --> 00:15:40.610
Yes, Leonhard?

00:15:40.610 --> 00:15:43.120
I don't really understand what
you're saying. It's too difficult.

00:15:43.120 --> 00:15:45.650
But you looked good saying it!

00:15:45.650 --> 00:15:47.040
Did that really necessitate
raising his hand?

00:15:47.370 --> 00:15:51.600
Heh. Don't worry. All you need
to do is follow my instructions.

00:15:51.600 --> 00:15:53.300
He's not displeased with that.

00:15:53.300 --> 00:15:55.820
First, we organize the items on the floor.

00:15:55.820 --> 00:15:57.820
Leonhard and I will handle the books.

00:15:57.820 --> 00:15:59.930
Licht and Kai, you see to the other items.

00:15:59.930 --> 00:16:00.680
You got it.

00:16:00.680 --> 00:16:02.730
All right. We'll pick up all the things!

00:16:03.610 --> 00:16:04.730
Maybe here?

00:16:04.730 --> 00:16:06.320
Stop, Leonhard.

00:16:06.320 --> 00:16:06.610
Huh?

00:16:06.800 --> 00:16:08.370
This is completely unacceptable!

00:16:08.820 --> 00:16:12.030
You order them by publisher,
series, and then author!

00:16:12.030 --> 00:16:15.620
Then, from right to left, the books
should go from tallest to shortest.

00:16:13.200 --> 00:16:15.140
This will not be over quickly.

00:16:15.620 --> 00:16:18.360
Jeez, Bruni, that's not right.

00:16:18.360 --> 00:16:21.280
First you've got to put things in the
general area where you want them.

00:16:21.280 --> 00:16:24.110
You can always move the
little things around later.

00:16:24.110 --> 00:16:26.030
It's almost like he's used to cleaning.

00:16:26.030 --> 00:16:29.230
Ah, Prince Licht.
Please do not touch that box.

00:16:29.230 --> 00:16:29.750
Huh?

00:16:29.750 --> 00:16:32.260
It is a private item.

00:16:32.550 --> 00:16:34.140
It will be fine here.

00:16:34.570 --> 00:16:35.570
Hmm? What is it?

00:16:35.570 --> 00:16:36.980
Ahem. Nothing.

00:16:36.980 --> 00:16:38.860
Master, please, return to your work.

00:16:38.860 --> 00:16:39.760
Very well.

00:16:40.640 --> 00:16:45.050
A private item, huh? If we look inside it,
maybe we can find out who he really is.

00:16:45.050 --> 00:16:48.250
Perhaps, but we certainly cannot
open it in front of him.

00:16:48.250 --> 00:16:50.140
Okay! I'll handle this.

00:16:50.140 --> 00:16:50.600
Huh?

00:16:50.600 --> 00:16:53.750
Whoa! Itchy! Itchy! My back is so itchy!

00:16:53.750 --> 00:16:55.740
Heine, scratch me! Quickly now!

00:16:55.940 --> 00:16:57.490
Err, as you wish.

00:16:57.730 --> 00:16:58.880
Prince Licht?

00:16:59.720 --> 00:17:03.010
Huh? What was I about to do?

00:17:03.010 --> 00:17:05.380
Oh, yeah! I'm thirsty.

00:17:05.380 --> 00:17:07.490
Professor, bring me something to drink.

00:17:07.490 --> 00:17:09.480
We can make tea here.

00:17:09.970 --> 00:17:10.890
Okay!

00:17:10.890 --> 00:17:12.570
Then go fetch me some sachertorte!

00:17:12.570 --> 00:17:15.760
You cannot ask Master to do such a
trivial task! I will go and get it!

00:17:15.760 --> 00:17:17.520
What's the point if <i>you</i> go?!

00:17:17.920 --> 00:17:22.190
I'm terribly sorry, but would you mind
putting off the tea until later?

00:17:22.190 --> 00:17:25.390
There's something I'd like
to finish up quickly.

00:17:33.990 --> 00:17:35.030
Stop that!

00:17:35.230 --> 00:17:36.440
What is this?

00:17:36.440 --> 00:17:40.830
A collection of letters my former
students gave me when we parted.

00:17:41.060 --> 00:17:44.760
Dear Professor Heine, thank you. I love you.

00:17:44.760 --> 00:17:48.930
I love studying now. Thank you.

00:17:48.930 --> 00:17:53.040
When I grow up, I want to be a
teacher like you, Professor Heine.

00:17:53.040 --> 00:17:53.990
This one says the same.

00:17:54.700 --> 00:17:57.930
One can tell that Master is a
man of incredible character.

00:17:58.220 --> 00:18:00.540
They loved your lessons.

00:18:00.540 --> 00:18:00.980
Ah!

00:18:01.540 --> 00:18:03.910
The presents we gave you are in here, too.

00:18:03.910 --> 00:18:05.080
But of course.

00:18:05.420 --> 00:18:10.320
All of my students are precious to me.

00:18:10.320 --> 00:18:12.310
Of course, that includes Your Highnesses.

00:18:12.310 --> 00:18:16.950
What's more, you all have great
individuality and it is truly rewarding to teach you.

00:18:16.950 --> 00:18:19.260
Every day since the first has been eventful.

00:18:19.260 --> 00:18:21.090
It has all been very worthwhile.

00:18:21.090 --> 00:18:24.930
I am grateful for the life I
have lived since meeting you.

00:18:25.270 --> 00:18:26.380
Heine...

00:18:26.380 --> 00:18:27.350
Master...

00:18:28.120 --> 00:18:29.950
Sorry for opening it.

00:18:29.950 --> 00:18:30.800
No matter.

00:18:31.190 --> 00:18:36.210
Now then, I will have to add even more
future lessons and homework to the stack...

00:18:36.610 --> 00:18:38.790
Ack, there's that much?!

00:18:38.790 --> 00:18:39.800
Argh...

00:18:39.800 --> 00:18:41.590
That is enough for our break.

00:18:41.590 --> 00:18:42.490
Yeah.

00:18:42.490 --> 00:18:46.870
Let us continue cleaning with
even more gratitude for Master!

00:18:46.870 --> 00:18:47.790
Let's do our best!

00:18:47.790 --> 00:18:49.100
We've got this!

00:18:58.820 --> 00:19:00.610
Professor, where do you want these?

00:19:00.610 --> 00:19:04.830
Ah, I borrowed those books from the royal library.
I've been meaning to return them.

00:19:05.130 --> 00:19:07.090
Okay, I'll take them back.

00:19:07.090 --> 00:19:09.660
By yourself? It's rather far.

00:19:09.660 --> 00:19:13.360
Leave it to me! I can take a workout!

00:19:13.360 --> 00:19:14.820
All right!

00:19:15.040 --> 00:19:18.550
You're such a muscle-head.
I could never ever do that.

00:19:19.040 --> 00:19:21.670
Don't praise me so much, little brother!

00:19:21.670 --> 00:19:22.810
That wasn't praise.

00:19:22.980 --> 00:19:25.760
Excuse me. Would you like
some tea, Professor?

00:19:25.760 --> 00:19:26.630
Huh?

00:19:26.850 --> 00:19:27.800
Huh?

00:19:31.840 --> 00:19:33.730
Hey, are you oka...

00:19:34.680 --> 00:19:36.140
Are you okay, Licht—

00:19:36.810 --> 00:19:38.410
Look out! The chair!

00:19:37.340 --> 00:19:39.250
I'll mop it up... need a rag...

00:19:37.470 --> 00:19:39.870
Kai, those are Master's sheets!

00:19:38.410 --> 00:19:39.700
Leo, open your eyes!

00:19:40.200 --> 00:19:42.600
I'm so sorry. I'll clean this up.

00:19:42.600 --> 00:19:46.460
No, it is all right.
We are fortunate no one was hurt.

00:19:46.460 --> 00:19:50.070
Yes, sir. I'm terribly sorry. Excuse me.

00:19:54.750 --> 00:19:55.880
Why?

00:19:56.140 --> 00:19:58.270
Why?!

00:19:58.270 --> 00:20:00.560
It is no use wondering why after the fact.

00:20:00.560 --> 00:20:02.930
I will help, as well.

00:20:04.300 --> 00:20:06.040
You need a lesson!

00:20:06.040 --> 00:20:08.720
Who do you think we were cleaning for?!

00:20:10.110 --> 00:20:12.510
Thankfully, the disaster did
not extend to your desk.

00:20:12.930 --> 00:20:16.440
Now, please continue your own work.

00:20:16.740 --> 00:20:19.410
All right! Professor Heine's
room cleaning squad!

00:20:19.410 --> 00:20:21.180
Our cleaning begins anew!

00:20:21.180 --> 00:20:23.060
Yeah!

00:20:44.440 --> 00:20:45.390
My word.

00:20:45.390 --> 00:20:48.900
What do you think, Master?
Maybe it's not enough yet.

00:20:48.900 --> 00:20:51.530
Oh, no. It is perfect, in my opinion.

00:20:51.530 --> 00:20:54.730
So, um, were we useful?

00:20:55.110 --> 00:20:57.730
Is this a proper thank-you?

00:21:00.690 --> 00:21:02.280
Yes. Of course.

00:21:02.280 --> 00:21:07.780
Thank you for working hard for me,
and for the tidy room.

00:21:08.090 --> 00:21:11.160
I will put on some tea as thanks.
Will you join me for it?

00:21:11.160 --> 00:21:11.830
Yeah!

00:21:11.830 --> 00:21:12.650
Sounds great.

00:21:12.650 --> 00:21:13.990
I would be honored.

00:21:13.990 --> 00:21:14.750
Okay.

00:21:15.410 --> 00:21:18.800
A sachertorte after hard work is the best.

00:21:18.800 --> 00:21:19.910
It's good.

00:21:19.920 --> 00:21:20.670
Yeah.

00:21:20.670 --> 00:21:23.070
Torte, torte.

00:21:23.070 --> 00:21:23.540
Hmm?

00:21:23.540 --> 00:21:27.040
Huh? Professor, you still had this?

00:21:27.250 --> 00:21:29.280
This rubbish article.

00:21:29.280 --> 00:21:31.800
"A criminal has slipped into the palace"?

00:21:31.800 --> 00:21:34.660
How outrageous.
That paper writes nothing but lies.

00:21:34.660 --> 00:21:36.510
Seriously! I hate liars!

00:21:36.510 --> 00:21:40.220
The people in the palace are all nice.
They're all good people.

00:21:40.450 --> 00:21:44.550
Ha, a criminal in the palace? Where
could they possibly slip in?

00:21:44.550 --> 00:21:47.020
Honestly! There's no way
a criminal would be here.

00:21:48.160 --> 00:21:49.970
You need a lesson!

00:21:50.630 --> 00:21:54.970
It is not good to assume what is true
without confirming it for yourself.

00:21:55.460 --> 00:22:00.530
What if the criminal was someone in the
palace who is nice to Your Highnesses?

00:22:00.770 --> 00:22:01.330
Huh?

00:22:04.200 --> 00:22:07.330
For example, what if it was me?

00:23:39.360 --> 00:23:41.810
Kai, why don't we play chess for a change?

00:23:41.810 --> 00:23:42.980
Okay. Let's play.

00:23:42.980 --> 00:23:45.320
Gah! There's dust on the chessboard!

00:23:45.320 --> 00:23:49.750
Wait a moment, Kai. We'll begin our match once
I've polished it until I can see my reflection!

00:23:46.570 --> 00:23:53.770
Next Time:
The Pair's Promise

00:23:49.750 --> 00:23:51.370
Next time, "The Pair's Promise."

00:23:51.370 --> 00:23:53.860
You really like things to
be clean. You're a good boy.
